schema: "0.3"
id: echo-of-manifestation-creature-hollow-parishioner
type: image
service: gemini

prompt:
  text: >
    Dark fantasy concept art of a Hollow Parishioner — an ambient enemy found in Zone 1,
    the Faded Chapel. A corrupted churchgoer in mid-prayer, kneeling on a dissolving pew
    in the half-materialized nave. The figure wears Sunday clothes from an indeterminate
    era — a dark suit or modest dress — but the fabric has fused with the chapel's shadow.
    Its posture is perpetual supplication: hands clasped, head bowed, knees on the pew's
    edge. The corruption manifests from the face: shadow pours from its eye sockets in
    thin streams that flow downward like black tears, pooling on the pew and dripping to
    the floor. The mouth hangs slightly open, also leaking shadow. Despite this, the figure
    maintains its prayer posture rigidly — it has been praying for centuries and will
    continue for centuries more. The parishioner is not aggressive by default — it exists
    in ambient prayer, but if disturbed by the player's transmutation resonance or direct
    interaction, it rises and attacks with slow but relentless determination. The background
    shows the Faded Chapel interior — amber candlelight, dissolving pews, indigo shadows.
    Painterly style, atmospheric candlelit lighting, the horror is in the familiar made
    uncanny — ordinary faith corrupted into eternal, hollow ritual.
  negative: "bright, cheerful, cartoon, anime, clean magic, zombie, skeleton, overt monster, running pose, colorful palette, modern clothing, low detail, flat shading, scary face"

output:
  formats:
    - format: png
  dimensions:
    width: 1024
    height: 1536
    aspect_ratio: "2:3"

tags: [creature, ambient-enemy, zone-1, parishioner, chapel, concept-art, dark-fantasy]
